          <groundspeak:finder id="1565005">Takin it Easy</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP445 Fairview

Posted: N56° 04.170 W118° 23.207

GPSr: N56° 04.170 W118° 23.209&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After our long drive back from Boundary Lake we had a few more caps to find before settling in for the night in Peace River.  This was a type of drive up cap that we have seen a few times in the past... in the grass at a street corner of a residential area.  Things were really quiet tonight and the find was easily recorded.  Thanks for the cap OFTH!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="247880644">
          <groundspeak:date>2012-07-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="836983">Coolcat21</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP445 Fairview?

Posted: N56 04.170  W118 23.207?

GPSr: N56 04.171  W118 23.209

?Elevation: 648m&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This was a quick find on my way through Fairview. Visiting Fairview brought back memories. Years ago I was part of a small delegation that was brought here by architects to see the way the College facilities were integrated into the community facilities, something that was going to happen in Tisdale, Saskatchewan. We flew all the way from Tisdale cheek to jowl in a small one engine plane. Quite the memory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the cap and the memories!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
